  "Description":          "Identifies the user's face in a Basic Visual Object. One SubAIM, Face Identity Recognition, and no code of its own. It exists so the User Agent can reach PAF-FIR without talking to an AIM: the UA writes a Basic Visual Object to a boundary port and the Controller routes it to FIR and the resulting Face Instance Identifier and Bounding Box back. The UAG prefix marks it as belonging to the User Agent rather than to MPAI-PAF.",
